<div class="section">

<h2>Project Overview</h2>

<p>

The <strong>Automated University Routine Generator (AURG)</strong> is a web-based academic scheduling system developed as an
Integrated Design Project – II (IDP-II) for the Department of Computer Science & Engineering,
University of Scholars.

The system automates the complex process of university timetable generation using
Artificial Intelligence techniques based on the <strong>Constraint Satisfaction Problem (CSP)</strong>.
Instead of manually preparing class schedules over several days, AURG intelligently generates
optimized, conflict-free routines within seconds while satisfying institutional scheduling constraints.

</p>

</div>

